                                "sense_id": "5eb9eb40-a3db-3b39-b10d-1bfe2b8fa779",
                                "text": "For two vague regions, one topological relation exists between any pair of crispings. There are a number of relations possible between the members of the sets of crisp regions on which the vague regions stand."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3d60b12d-9bcb-38aa-8ec4-a206be92a36a",
